Piggy-backed Queries Attack
Attack Principle: Use semicolon separator to execute multiple SQL statements, appending malicious operations
Feature Detection:
Semicolon separator:
Check for ; separating multiple SQL statements
Destructive statements:
DELETE FROM ...
DROP TABLE ..., DROP DATABASE ...
TRUNCATE TABLE ...
Data manipulation statements:
INSERT INTO ...
UPDATE ... SET ...
CREATE TABLE ... AS SELECT ...
ALTER TABLE ...
Stored procedure operations:
CREATE PROCEDURE ...
CALL procedure_name(...)
DROP PROCEDURE IF EXISTS ...
EXEC ..., EXECUTE ...
Judgment Points:
Whether multiple SQL statements exist
Whether subsequent statements are destructive or unauthorized
Whether these operations exceed normal business scope